Third-party dependencies
================================================================================

Tracks depends on, but does not vendor, a number of separately licensed
projects. Their licenses apply to those components:

  go-pmtiles / PMTiles     BSD-3-Clause
  Protomaps basemap        BSD-3-Clause / ODbL (OpenStreetMap data)
  MapLibre GL JS           BSD-3-Clause
  MapLibre Native          BSD-2-Clause
  tippecanoe               BSD-2-Clause
  Bouncy Castle            MIT-style (bouncycastle.org licence)
  Caddy                    Apache-2.0
  PostgreSQL               PostgreSQL License
  Redis                    BSD-3-Clause / RSALv2
  FastAPI, SQLAlchemy,     MIT / BSD / Apache-2.0
    Celery, React, Vite,
    Tailwind, Recharts

Map data is © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database
License (ODbL). Elevation data derives from public-domain and openly licensed
national DEM sources.

The Android app composes libsodium's sealed box from Bouncy Castle primitives
(mobile/core/src/jvmSharedMain/.../BouncyCastleIngestCrypto.kt) rather than
binding libsodium itself. The wire format is fixed by the server's PyNaCl, and
every Android binding of libsodium ships a prebuilt .so — which F-Droid does not
accept. The implementation is checked against a ciphertext produced by PyNaCl,
in both directions.

Note: the backend currently depends on garmin-fit-sdk, which Garmin
distributes under the Flexible and Interoperable Data Transfer (FIT) Protocol
License rather than an OSI-approved free software license. It is a runtime
dependency of the server only; it is not vendored, and it is not a dependency
of the mobile app.
